                    <occupation>author, newspaper journalist</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p> Felix MacCarthy is referenced 15 times in the diary between 1794 to
                            1809. He was a journalist for the Orcale and the Albion newspaper. It is
                            worth noting that in later references to meetings with MacCarthy,
                            08.03.1807 and 01.01.1807, they meet unexpectedly ('adv.'), with
                            Hippisley present at both. There is some dispute over whether or not he
                            went to prison at the same time as Gerald. Little is known of his life
                            beyond 1801.</p>
